#### Example 5: Azure Policy — Continuous Cloud Configuration Invariant

For Azure-hosted services, Azure Policy provides cloud-native compliance evaluation that runs on every resource change — faster than daily drift detection:

```json
{
  "displayName": "Gainwell HIPAA: Storage accounts must have HTTPS-only traffic enabled",
  "description": "Enforces the GP-001 INF-001 infrastructure invariant at the Azure platform level. Non-compliant storage accounts are flagged for remediation.",
  "policyType": "Custom",
  "mode": "All",
  "metadata": {
    "category": "Gainwell HIPAA Compliance",
    "goldenPathCheck": "INF-001",
    "verificationLayer": "4",
    "owner": "platform-engineering@gainwell.com"
  },
  "parameters": {
    "effect": {
      "type": "String",
      "defaultValue": "Audit",
      "allowedValues": ["Audit", "Deny", "Disabled"]
    }
  },
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {
          "field": "type",
          "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"
        },
        {
          "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/supportsHttpsTrafficOnly",
          "notEquals": "true"
        }
      ]
    },
    "then": {
      "effect": "[parameters('effect')]"
    }
  }
}
```

**Assignment configuration (Terraform):**
```hcl
resource "azurerm_policy_assignment" "hipaa_https_only" {
  name                 = "gainwell-hipaa-https-only"
  scope                = data.azurerm_subscription.current.id
  policy_definition_id = azurerm_policy_definition.hipaa_https_only.id
  display_name         = "Gainwell HIPAA: Enforce HTTPS-only storage"

  parameters = jsonencode({
    effect = { value = "Audit" }  # Use 'Deny' for newly-created resources once all existing resources compliant
  })
}
```

**Integration with Compliance Evidence Store:** Azure Policy compliance state is exported daily via:
```bash
az policy state list \
  --filter "policyAssignmentName eq 'gainwell-hipaa-https-only'" \
  --select 'resourceId,complianceState,timestamp,policyDefinitionId' \
  | jq '[.[] | {check_id: "INF-001", resource: .resourceId, result: .complianceState, timestamp: .timestamp}]' \
  | python scripts/export-cloud-policy-to-evidence-store.py
```
